{
 "schema": 2,
 "name": "foilsflash_bc",
 "note": "foilsflash_ax on SimJob MDC2025bc, with the IPA and OPA in place: its knobs, geometry, objectives and flash budget are foilsflash_ax's. It also carries foilsnopa_bc's per-design tracker hit rates as saved columns, the reference for foilsnopa_bc and for Production's pileup. The busiest-channel tracker rate is edep_occupancy_combine's busiest region (12 planes x 8 straw numbers x the six panels, the mean per straw; unbiased at a design point's statistics, unlike a single row) in the digitizers' event window, from three pileup components each normalized per generated event (gen_events_per_pot) at 1.58e7 POT per microbunch; the beam-flash neutrons and gammas are left out. Design: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-30-foilsnopa-study-design.md, revision 2026-11-05 (local).",
 "knobs": [
  {
   "name": "extra_rOut_up",
   "type": "real",
   "min": 50.0,
   "max": 250.0,
   "unit": "",
   "fmt": "{:.4f}"
  },
  {
   "name": "extra_rOut_dn",
   "type": "real",
   "min": 50.0,
   "max": 250.0,
   "unit": "",
   "fmt": "{:.4f}"
  },
  {
   "name": "extra_halfThickness_up",
   "type": "real",
   "min": 0.002,
   "max": 1.0,
   "unit": "",
   "fmt": "{:.6f}"
  },
  {
   "name": "extra_halfThickness_dn",
   "type": "real",
   "min": 0.002,
   "max": 1.0,
   "unit": "",
   "fmt": "{:.6f}"
  },
  {
   "name": "extra_f_up",
   "type": "real",
   "min": 0.0,
   "max": 0.95,
   "unit": "",
   "fmt": "{:.4f}"
  },
  {
   "name": "extra_f_dn",
   "type": "real",
   "min": 0.0,
   "max": 0.95,
   "unit": "",
   "fmt": "{:.4f}"
  }
 ],
 "derive": {
  "consts": {
   "n_up": 6,
   "n_dn": 6,
   "base_n": 37,
   "base_rOut": 75.0,
   "base_hT": 0.0528,
   "base_hole": 21.5
  },
  "exprs": {
   "rIn_up": "extra_f_up * extra_rOut_up",
   "rIn_dn": "extra_f_dn * extra_rOut_dn"
  },
  "profiles": {}
 },
 "geom": {
  "writer": "offline_simpleconfig",
  "base": "Offline/Mu2eG4/geom/geom_run1_a.txt",
  "lines": [
   {
    "comment": "=== foilsflash (6D, hole = fraction of that side's rOut) ==="
   },
   {
    "comment": "{base_n} base foils (DOE-2017, rOut={base_rOut}, hT={base_hT}, holeRadius={base_hole})"
   },
   {
    "comment": "+ {n_up} up at (rOut={extra_rOut_up:.2f}, hT={extra_halfThickness_up:.4f}, rIn={rIn_up:.2f})"
   },
   {
    "comment": "+ {n_dn} dn at (rOut={extra_rOut_dn:.2f}, hT={extra_halfThickness_dn:.4f}, rIn={rIn_dn:.2f})"
   },
   {
    "comment": "holeRadii vector decouples extras-rIn from base-rIn (patched lib)."
   },
   {
    "comment": "EMC_Source relocated 5300 -> 5000. It is a 20um disc of ds.vacuumMaterial (vd.halfLength=0.01) -- ZERO mass, no scattering, no absorption -- and NO foils-family stage reads virtual detectors (only pot_only instantiates ReadVirtualDetector). At 5300 it was the UPSTREAM wall of the zero-overlap corridor, capping the stack at 6271-5300=971mm. zEMCSourceInMu2e is a plain c.getDouble default at VirtualDetectorMaker.cc:189, so this is one config line, no source patch. EMC_Source2 stays at 4800, so ordering is preserved."
   },
   {
    "key": "zEMCSourceInMu2e",
    "type": "double",
    "value": 5000.0
   },
   {
    "comment": "protonabsorber.distFromTargetEnd 491.666672 (stock 625). This line's 49 foils span 1066.67 mm vs the deployed 800, so its downstream end sits 133.33 mm further back, and Offline slides the IPA the same 133.33 mm downstream with it -- as a RIGID body: length stays 1000 mm because pabs1halflen saturates at the protonabsorber.halfLength=500 cap. Measured with protonabsorber.verbosityLevel=1: stock 6901.02-7901.02, uncompensated 7034.35-8034.35, compensated 6901.02-7901.02. The IPA is FIXED HARDWARE at z=6901-7901, so that displacement was a physics error present in all 414 historical rows, not just an overlap. Compensating restores the absorber to its true position AND removes the overlap, with the target left at its original z0."
   },
   {
    "key": "protonabsorber.distFromTargetEnd",
    "type": "double",
    "value": 491.666672
   },
   {
    "key": "hasTSdA",
    "type": "bool",
    "value": false
   },
   {
    "key": "tsda.helical.build",
    "type": "bool",
    "value": false
   },
   {
    "key": "stoppingTarget.radii",
    "type": "vector<double>",
    "fmt": "{:.4f}",
    "segments": [
     {
      "count": "n_up",
      "expr": "extra_rOut_up"
     },
     {
      "count": "base_n",
      "expr": "base_rOut"
     },
     {
      "count": "n_dn",
      "expr": "extra_rOut_dn"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "key": "stoppingTarget.halfThicknesses",
    "type": "vector<double>",
    "fmt": "{:.6f}",
    "segments": [
     {
      "count": "n_up",
      "expr": "extra_halfThickness_up"
     },
     {
      "count": "base_n",
      "expr": "base_hT"
     },
     {
      "count": "n_dn",
      "expr": "extra_halfThickness_dn"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "comment": "POISON PILL: an unpatched StoppingTargetMaker ignores holeRadii and reads"
   },
   {
    "comment": "this scalar. 1e6 forces a loud G4Tubs crash instead of a silently uniform"
   },
   {
    "comment": "stack -- emitting a 'sensible' scalar is how 62 foilsg rows were lost."
   },
   {
    "key": "stoppingTarget.holeRadius",
    "type": "double",
    "raw": "1.0e6"
   },
   {
    "key": "stoppingTarget.holeRadii",
    "type": "vector<double>",
    "fmt": "{:.4f}",
    "segments": [
     {
      "count": "n_up",
      "expr": "rIn_up"
     },
     {
      "count": "base_n",
      "expr": "base_hole"
     },
     {
      "count": "n_dn",
      "expr": "rIn_dn"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "comment": "Degrader parked at 120 deg (mmackenz hardware detent)"
   },
   {
    "key": "degrader.build",
    "type": "bool",
    "value": false
   },
   {
    "key": "degrader.rotation",
    "type": "double",
    "value": 120.0
   },
   {
    "key": "ts.coll5.material1Name",
    "type": "string",
    "value": "COL5Poly"
   },
   {
    "comment": "TT_MidInner -> DS2Vacuum workaround REMOVED 2026-07-28 (Run1Bap migration). Under v13_12_10 constructVirtualDetectors:502 parented the tracker VDs on `isDumbbell` (always false here), nailing them into DS2Vacuum while Mu2eWorld:346 put the tracker itself in DS3Vacuum -- VDs protruded 1.8-3.5 m outside their mother, GeomMgt0002 fatal. Forcing tracker.inDS2Vacuum=true + ds2.halfLength=3825 made the two agree. v13_32_10 keys VD parenting on !tracker.inDS2Vacuum, so stock is self-consistent and the workaround is not just redundant but harmful: it re-parented EMC_0_Front into DS2Vacuum as a sibling of StoppingTargetMother, which WAS the last remaining overlap. Measured 2x2 on foilspf corner_hi: Run1Bak+override 1 overlap, Run1Bap+override 1, Run1Bak-override 6 + rc=134 core dump, Run1Bap-override 0."
   },
   {
    "key": "ds.hasServicePipes",
    "type": "bool",
    "value": false
   },
   {
    "comment": "Overlap-suppression (foil-support off + rail shrink)"
   },
   {
    "key": "stoppingTarget.foilTarget_supportStructure",
    "type": "bool",
    "value": false
   },
   {
    "key": "ds.lengthRail2",
    "type": "double",
    "value": 0.1
   },
   {
    "key": "ds.lengthRail3",
    "type": "double",
    "value": 0.1
   }
  ]
 },
 "kits": {
